{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And the flesh of the bull.</b> This bull of sin-offering was to atone for the deed of the calf. And it mentions 'it shall be burned with fire' in the same sense as the burning of the red heifer, and its secret is known from the sent-away goat. And the leaning by the sons — as it says, ״וסמך אהרן ובניו״ — is because the Holy One, blessed be He, grew wrathful against Aaron to destroy him, and it was mollified by the sons; therefore they needed to obtain atonement through him."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:18.882375406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}